0012: `_SFLOAT` members in the integer UBWC compat classes.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: not sent - upstream's
`"a630 blob allows these, but not a660"` is deliberate (a660 is this gen2
family), so the patch argues from layouts, not from the blob, and that is what an
upstream reviewer would have to accept.
**Found:** 04.10, probe `U` (promoted from
`experiments/exp-8-sfloat-int-ubwc-compat.patch`): five vkd3d TYPELESS classes
mixed `_SFLOAT` with integers and lost compression entirely.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. A `R32_TYPELESS`-shaped texture with an integer and a float view
in one list keeps UBWC instead of dropping it.

## Summary

Stock keeps every `_FLOAT` out of `fd6_ubwc_compat_mode()`, and one unknown member
clears `ubwc_enabled` for the whole list. But an `_SFLOAT` member has exactly the
same layout as the integer member of the same typeless format (same bits per
channel, same swizzle, same tiled markup); a Vulkan cast reinterprets bits, it
does not permute channels. With the classes added, the vkd3d classes that hold
UBWC on stock go 31 -> 36. `Z32_FLOAT` stays `UNKNOWN`: it belongs to no colour
typeless family, and depth has its own clear semantics.

## Evidence

One hunk in `freedreno_ubwc.h`. Probe `U` of `tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c`:
stock `list=0x100000` against `nonmut=0x102000` (the list dropped UBWC), with the
patch `list=0x102000`; roundtrip through all three shapes EXACT 0/262144. Isolated
A/B on the 0005-0010 stack: 5 lines of probe output move
(`results/test-stack.log` vs `results/test-0012.log`), and
`results/test-backup-oct2.log` matches the stack+patch run byte for byte.

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| the five TYPELESS classes keep UBWC | probe `U` memreq, journal 20.5 | `0x100000 -> 0x102000` |
| the contents still round-trip | probe `U` copy roundtrip | EXACT 0/262144 in all shapes |
| nothing else moves | probes `S`, `T`; the 94-row matrix, journal 24.3 | PASS; 94 EXACT |

Risk that stays: the driver never compares UBWC fast-clear metadata against the
format interpretation, so a fast-clear through a float view is unchecked by a
byte roundtrip. That is stated, not fixed.

## The change in this repo

One hunk, integer classes only; it must not admit a float member of a class that
has no integer member. Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name explicit.

## Related

`0006`, `0011` (same switch); `experiments/exp-8`; journal 32 (the same layout
argument for the two 64-bit labels).

